  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:51075",
  "description": "gpsd is a service daemon that mediates access to a GPS sensor connected to the host computer by serial or USB interface, making its data on the location/course/velocity of the sensor available to be queried on TCP port 2947 of the host computer. With gpsd, multiple GPS client applications (such as navigational and war-driving software) can share access to a GPS without contention or loss of data. Also, gpsd responds to queries with a format that is substantially easier to parse than NMEA 0183. The AlmaLinux support for this package is limited. See \u003chttps://access.AlmaLinux.com/support/policy/gpsd-support\u003e for more details.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * gpsd: gpsd: Command Injection via GPS device subtype allows arbitrary code execution (CVE-2026-58459)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
